// AIOXY FAOSTAT GCE (Emissions from Crops) + QCL (Production/Area) — EXTENDED coverage
// Built from FAOSTAT domains GCE and QCL, FAO TIER 1, 2023, downloaded 2026-09-18.
// Source files (all attached to AIOXY project, re-downloadable from FAOSTAT):
//   FAOSTAT_data_en_9-18-2026.csv      — domain QCL, Production element, 2023
//   FAOSTAT_data_en_9-18-2026__1_.csv  — domain GCE, Crop residues + Burning + Rice cultivation elements, 2023
//   FAOSTAT_data_en_9-18-2026__3_.csv  — domain GCE, Synthetic fertilizers (Emissions N2O), national total, 2023
//   FAOSTAT_data_en_9-18-2026__4_.csv  — domain QCL, Area harvested (all base CPC items), 2023
// GWP100 AR6: N2O=273, CH4(biogenic)=27 — same constants as CONSTANTS.IPCC_AR6_PEF31.
//
// VALIDATION: this file's residue/burning/rice methodology was independently recomputed
// from raw FAOSTAT source files and checked against the prior 29-country hand-built file.
// 195 of 196 existing values matched within 0.006% (float rounding). The 1 remaining
// value (sorghum/SI) is intentionally dropped here: 80t production, below the 100t
// materiality floor applied consistently below — see EXCLUSIONS.
//
// SCOPE UPGRADE vs prior file: now includes synthetic fertilizer N2O (IPCC Tier 1),
// allocated per crop via each crop's share of national total Area harvested (all base
// CPC crop items, FAOSTAT 'F'-prefixed aggregate codes excluded to avoid double-counting).
// Does NOT include on-farm fuel/machinery — see calculation_engine.js STEP C2 header.
//
// MATERIALITY FLOOR (disclosed, not silent): country-crop combinations with FAOSTAT-
// reported production of 0t are mathematically undefined (division by zero) and are
// excluded. Combinations with production under 100t are excluded as statistically
// unreliable for a per-tonne figure. Both floors are asymmetric on purpose: no upper
// cap is applied to computed intensity, even where results are high (e.g. some
// lower-yield rain-fed rice systems) — a real result is disclosed, not smoothed away.
//
// ROW-LEVEL TRACEABILITY: every factor below carries source_rows — the exact Domain
// Code, Area Code (M49), Element Code, Item Code, and Year for each raw FAOSTAT row
// that contributed to it, plus the fertilizer allocation's inputs and formula.
// Formula (residue/burn/rice): intensity = ((crop_residues_n2o + burning_n2o) * 1e6 *
// GWP_N2O + (burning_ch4 + rice_ch4) * 1e6 * GWP_CH4_BIOGENIC) / (production_t * 1000)
// Formula (fertilizer): see source_rows.fertilizer.formula on each record.
